# Response headers for Cloudflare Pages. Copied verbatim into the build output
# by the asset glob in apps/web/project.json.
#
# Deliberately absent:
#
# - Content-Security-Policy. Angular emits inline styles, and analytics injects
#   a googletagmanager script only after consent, so a correct policy needs
#   measuring rather than guessing. A wrong one fails silently in production and
#   nowhere else, which is worse than not having one yet.
# - Strict-Transport-Security. HSTS is remembered by browsers for its whole
#   max-age, so it is a semi-sticky commitment that belongs on Cloudflare's own
#   TLS settings page where it can be turned off again, not in a file that ships
#   with a build.

# PRE-LAUNCH ONLY: the `X-Robots-Tag: noindex` line below. Remove it and flip
# SEARCH_INDEXABLE in apps/web/src/app/site.ts on the day the site launches - a
# test fails while the two disagree, so neither can be forgotten on its own.
#
# The site is deployed before its screenshots and video exist, and a domain
# appears in Certificate Transparency logs within hours of its certificate being
# issued, which is how crawlers find new sites. Without this, the placeholder
# version of the documentation is what gets indexed, and removing a page from
# search results takes far longer than keeping it out.
#
# robots.txt deliberately still allows crawling: a disallowed crawler never
# reads this header, and Google will happily index a URL it was told not to
# fetch. Allow the fetch, refuse the indexing.

/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=(), payment=(), usb=()

# Every emitted script and stylesheet carries a content hash in its filename
# (`outputHashing: "all"`), so a given URL can never change contents.
/*.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*.css
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
